able name to logs (as in "log_path.exe_name.pid").\x00' 0x2a0@0x155d0|0x154a5=b'log_suffix\x00' 0x2a4@0x18488|0x1833c=b'String to append to log file name, e.g. ".txt".\x00' 0x2d4@0x11058|0x11060=b'log_to_syslog\x00' 0x2d8@0x17b57|0x17a0b=b'Write all sanitizer output to syslog in addition to other means of logging.\x00' 0x308@0x114f6|0x114fe=b'verbosity\x00' 0x30c@0x1e45d|0x1e299=b'Verbosity level (0 - silent, 1 - a bit of output, 2+ - more output).\x00' 0x33c@0x1931d|0x191e2=b'strip_env\x00' 0x340@0x12891|0x1288f=b'Whether to remove the sanitizer from DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES to avoid passing it to children on Apple platforms. Default is true.\x00' 0x370@0x142bd|0x141c5=b'verify_interceptors\x00' 0x374@0x12911|0x1290f=b'Verify that interceptors are working on Apple platforms. Default is true.\x00' 0x3a4@0x17ba3|0x17a57=b'detect_leaks\x00' 0x3a8@0x17bb0|0x17a64=b'Enable memory leak detection.\x00' 0x3d8@0x14d99|0x14ca1=b'leak_check_at_exit\x00' 0x3dc@0x142d1|0x141d9=b'Invoke leak checking in an atexit handler. Has no effect if detect_leaks=false, or if __lsan_do_leak_check() is called before the handler has a chance to run.\x00' 0x40c@0x17073|0x16f4f=b'allocator_may_return_null\x00' 0x410@0x1218f|0x12197=b'If false, the allocator will crash instead of returning 0 on out-of-memory.\x00' 0x440@0x1d611|0x1d45a=b'print_summary\x00' 0x444@0x14370|0x14278=b'If false, disable printing error summaries in addition to error reports.\x00' 0x474@0x13b94|0x13a9c=b'print_module_map\x00' 0x478@0x1c5e2|0x1c44d=b"Print the process module map where supported (0 - don't print, 1 - print only once before process exits, 2 - print after each report).\x00" 0x4a8@0x1e4a2|0x1e2de=b'check_printf\x00' 0x4ac@0x1cd6f|0x1cbc7=b'Check printf arguments.\x00' 0x4e4@0x16cd9|0x16ba5=b'handle_segv\x00' 0x4e8@0x1eddb|0x1ec17=b"Controls custom tool's SIGSEGV handler (0 - do not registers the handler, 1 - register the handler and allow user to set own, 2 - registers the handler and block user from changing i